'''Tibidon Station'''<ref name="Vintage">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: The Vintage Collection|packtype=Special Action Figure Set|pack=#257-259: ''Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi'' (Obi-Wan Kenobi, Teeka, & Purge Trooper)|altlink=https://www.banthaskull.com/story/news-official-reveal-the-vintage-collection-star-wars-obi-wan-kenobi-multipack}}</ref> also known as '''Sandwhale Farm''',<ref name="Return">''[[Obi-Wan Kenobi: A Jedi's Return]]''</ref> was a sand whaling station<ref name="KenobiIAD">{{Kenobi|Part I}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> active on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] during the [[Imperial Era]]. [[Jedi Master]]-in-[[Exile (punishment)|exile]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] worked at the station, helping to cut pieces from the<ref name="Part I" /> [[tibidon sand whale]] carcass as part of the makeshift operation.<ref name="KenobiITrivia">{{SW|url=obi-wan-kenobi-part-i-trivia-gallery|text=Part I Trivia Gallery &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}}</ref> The minimum wage for a full shift at the station paid one [[trugut]] and three [[wupiupi]].<ref name="Elegant weapon">{{SW|url=news/inside-the-lucasfilm-archive-obi-wan-kenobi-props-1|text=Inside the Lucasfilm Archive: An Elegant Weapon and Other Jedi Artifacts from the ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' Limited Series}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:TibidonStationBTS.png|thumb|right|220px|Ewan McGregor and Deborah Chow on the Tibidon Station set]]
Tibidon Station was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series, which was released on [[March 9]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|TWTfhyvzTx0|Obi-Wan Kenobi &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/teaser-trailer-obi-wan-kenobi}}</ref> It first appeared in the [[Part I|first episode]] of the series, which aired on [[May 26]], 2022.<ref name="Episode 1 Premiere">{{Twitter|obiwankenobi|status/1530019678562549760|''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''|quote=The time for #ObiWanKenobi has arrived&hellip;early. Start streaming the first two episodes on @DisneyPlus TONIGHT at 9PM PT.|archivedate=20220527053945}}</ref> It was first identified in a [[StarWars.com]] article announcing merchandise from the series, which was published on [[June 1]], 2022.<ref name="Wednesday">{{SW|url=news/obi-wan-wednesdays-week-2|text=Obi-Wan Wednesdays: Find Ben Kenobi at Tibidon Station and More!}}</ref> It was first identified as Sandwhale Farm in the documentary ''[[Obi-Wan Kenobi: A Jedi's Return]]'',<ref name="Return" /> which was released on [[September 8]], 2022.<ref name="Hello There">{{SW|url=news/obi-wan-kenobi-a-jedis-return|text=Hello There: ''Obi-Wan Kenobi: A Jedi's Return'' Documentary Coming on Disney+ Day}}</ref>

Director [[Deborah Chow]] and the crew looked at references of old whaling stations for the Sandwhale Farm, and it was her favorite set. On the first day of production, [[Ewan McGregor]], the actor who played Kenobi, starting filming his scenes in the set.<ref name="Return" /> Propmaster [[Brad Elliott]] and [[Lucasfilm]] creative executive [[Pablo Hidalgo]] discussed the wupiupi coins' proper conversion rate with truguts and [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], allowing the two to figure out the cost of some common goods in ''[[Star Wars]]'' and a minimum wage for the whale-carving station.<ref name="Elegant weapon" />

